WEBVTT

00:03.242 --> 00:04.436
Oh, oh, that is so true.

00:04.610 --> 00:08.205
I know exactly what you mean.
Oh, hang on, I'll get you an ashtray.

00:08.380 --> 00:11.178
- Oh, hey, Charlie.
- Hey, what's going on?

00:11.583 --> 00:14.381
Oh, I have a friend over
from my single-parent support group.

00:14.753 --> 00:18.746
Oh, yeah, unattached moms.
I gotta check out that group.

00:20.159 --> 00:23.720
- But you don't have a kid.
- Are they really strict about that?

00:25.397 --> 00:29.265
Because at the dog park, you show up with
a leash and say, "That's him by the tree. "

00:30.369 --> 00:33.566
It's a single-parent group.
You need to be a single parent.

00:33.739 --> 00:35.866
Seems a little prejudiced if you ask me.

00:37.209 --> 00:40.701
Hey, Alan, can I use your bathroom,
or should I just pee off the deck?

00:40.879 --> 00:42.540
Heh, it's right down the hall.

00:42.714 --> 00:45.410
Oh, uh, Greg, uh, this is
my brother, Charlie. Charlie, Greg.

00:45.584 --> 00:46.846
Hey.
- Hey, nice place.

00:47.019 --> 00:48.646
Thanks.

00:50.389 --> 00:52.482
She's a little butch for you, isn't she?

00:53.092 --> 00:56.391
Greg is a divorced dad.
He's got a daughter around Jake's age.

00:56.562 --> 00:58.587
Well, you can understand my confusion.

00:59.264 --> 01:01.289
You think I joined a group
to pick up women?

01:01.467 --> 01:05.062
No, I think you joined a support group
because you're a whiny little wuss.

01:06.472 --> 01:09.168
But as long as you're there,
you might as well nail a few.

01:10.375 --> 01:13.640
- Sex is not what the group's about.
- Oh, grow up.

01:13.812 --> 01:16.838
You put single men and women
on chairs in a church basement...

01:17.015 --> 01:19.142
...they're gonna start mounting
each other.

01:20.486 --> 01:24.081
The depths of your degeneracy
continue to astound me.

01:24.256 --> 01:26.588
Really? Still?

01:27.025 --> 01:30.791
So, Charlie, I'm guessing by the stack
of racing forms next to the can...

01:30.963 --> 01:32.954
...you bet the ponies.
- Hey, I'd bet on rabbits...

01:33.132 --> 01:34.497
...if you could get them organized.

01:36.335 --> 01:39.168
Is there a story behind that riding crop
hanging on the wall?

01:39.338 --> 01:43.104
Oh, yeah, that's a souvenir from a
wonderful weekend in Louisville, Kentucky.

01:43.275 --> 01:46.267
- Oh, you went to the Derby?
- No, it was a Hilton by the airport.

01:48.180 --> 01:52.082
- How about you? Do you hit the track?
- It's actually my second-biggest expense...

01:52.251 --> 01:55.709
...after alimony.
- So all your money goes to the nags, huh?

01:57.256 --> 01:59.724
- Hey, your brother's funny.
- At first.

02:01.193 --> 02:03.058
I'll get us some more beers.

02:03.228 --> 02:04.957
Charlie, you smoke cigars?

02:05.564 --> 02:07.691
I'd smoke rabbits
if you could keep them lit.

02:11.737 --> 02:16.174
- So divorced dad, huh?
- Yep.

02:16.909 --> 02:19.173
- How long were you married?
- Sixteen years.

02:19.344 --> 02:20.504
Whoa.

02:20.679 --> 02:23.147
What ended it? Cheating? Drinking?
Gambling?

02:25.050 --> 02:26.642
Gay.

02:28.554 --> 02:32.422
- Oh, her?
- No.

02:36.595 --> 02:37.960
Ah, ahem.

02:40.365 --> 02:43.425
So, what, you didn't wanna
try drinking or gambling?

02:52.477 --> 02:54.604
So, what about you, Charlie?
Ever been married?

02:54.780 --> 02:57.977
Ha, are you kidding? My brother
is definitely not the marrying kind.

02:58.217 --> 03:03.086
- Oh? Confirmed bachelor.
- No, no, nothing's confirmed.

03:03.689 --> 03:06.283
I mean, I just think variety
is the spice of life.

03:06.458 --> 03:10.087
And as far as spices go, some people
like salt, some people like pepper...

03:10.262 --> 03:13.595
...some people like salt and pepper.
Me, I like women. Ahem.

03:17.102 --> 03:19.195
Me too. Some of my best friends
are women.

03:19.371 --> 03:21.999
No, no, don't... Don't misunderstand.

03:22.374 --> 03:24.103
None of my friends are women.

03:24.276 --> 03:27.177
- Oh, I see.
- No, you don't.

03:27.346 --> 03:30.474
Oh, damn. I have to take a rain check
on that beer. I gotta get going.

03:30.649 --> 03:32.674
Oh, oh, okay. Uh, we still on for Sunday?

03:32.851 --> 03:34.978
Looking forward to it.
Really nice meeting you.

03:35.153 --> 03:37.849
- I'll see you at the track sometime.
- You never know.

03:38.023 --> 03:40.617
- Santa Anita or Hollywood Park?
- Which one do you like?

03:40.792 --> 03:43.454
- Oh, I'll go either way.
- Apparently.

03:44.196 --> 03:46.289
Oh, he's bad.

03:46.465 --> 03:48.729
You have no idea.

03:49.234 --> 03:51.395
- Okay, so I'll see you Sunday.
- Bye-bye.

03:51.570 --> 03:52.662
Adios.

03:52.838 --> 03:56.330
- Great guy, huh?
- Yeah, yeah, terrific.

03:56.575 --> 04:00.511
- How much do you know about him?
- Well, I know he's a successful architect...

04:00.679 --> 04:05.343
...his daughter's a soccer player, he's gay,
he has a boat, he went to UC Berkeley...

04:05.517 --> 04:07.576
okay, okay, back up a little.

04:08.186 --> 04:11.485
Oh, it's a sailboat.
Well, it's more of a sloop. He's...

04:12.024 --> 04:15.221
- He's taking me and Jake out on Sunday.
- No, no, no, one more.

04:15.394 --> 04:17.385
What? He's gay? What about it?

04:18.163 --> 04:20.859
Nothing, I'm just looking out for you.

04:22.267 --> 04:24.929
I mean, does he wanna take you sailing,
or does he wanna take you...

04:25.103 --> 04:26.695
...sailing?

04:31.510 --> 04:33.375
Don't be silly. He knows I'm not gay.

04:33.879 --> 04:35.710
Are you sure?

04:35.881 --> 04:38.441
For 16 years, he didn't know he was gay.

04:39.051 --> 04:42.418
You don't believe two men can be friends,
just because one of them is gay?

04:42.988 --> 04:45.855
It has nothing to do with gay.

04:46.024 --> 04:49.983
Imagine he were a straight guy
and you were an attractive young woman.

04:50.162 --> 04:53.290
- Do you think you could just be friends?
- How attractive?

04:54.833 --> 04:56.061
What?

04:56.234 --> 05:00.261
I mean, uh, you know, am I kind of cute
in a tomboy sort of way...

05:00.439 --> 05:03.533
...or am I smoking hot and working it?

05:07.312 --> 05:10.611
Okay, okay, let's start again.

05:11.283 --> 05:14.719
Imagine you were a straight guy.

05:16.755 --> 05:19.155
- And...?
- No "and. " That's it.

05:25.330 --> 05:28.128
Berta, how long have you
been working for me?

05:28.300 --> 05:30.325
Define "working. "

05:31.403 --> 05:33.337
What kind of hair conditioner do I use?

05:35.006 --> 05:36.268
I quit.

05:39.177 --> 05:43.580
I use a wash-out conditioner, then blow-dry
with a dab of styling gel.

05:43.749 --> 05:46.217
But you got me a leave-in conditioner.

05:46.385 --> 05:48.148
Why would you get
leave-in conditioner?

05:48.653 --> 05:50.177
- The truth?
- Please.

05:50.355 --> 05:52.186
It came with a free Lady Schick.

05:53.291 --> 05:55.282
Berta, my hair is important to me.

05:55.460 --> 05:57.985
All right, don't get your panties
in a bunch.

05:58.163 --> 05:59.824
What is that supposed to mean?

05:59.998 --> 06:01.829
It means don't get so agitated...

06:02.000 --> 06:05.265
...that your undergarments
become entangled within your crack.

06:07.339 --> 06:10.831
Hey, hey, hey. I am not agitated,
I just like having extra body without...

06:11.009 --> 06:13.739
...you know, stiffness.

06:18.583 --> 06:22.849
Okay, why don't you guys hang outside
while we throw together some lunch?

06:23.021 --> 06:24.613
Okay. Come on, Sophie.

06:24.790 --> 06:27.281
- This is a cool house.
- Yeah, it's my weekend place.

06:27.459 --> 06:29.654
I have a second home in the valley.

06:30.228 --> 06:33.322
- I think they like each other.
- Oh, Jake is smitten.

06:33.498 --> 06:37.559
I usually only see that look on his face
when we go to the pancake house.

06:39.070 --> 06:40.230
- Hey.
- Hi, Charlie.

06:40.405 --> 06:43.169
- Hey, how'd the sailing go?
- Oh, great. Perfect weather.

06:43.341 --> 06:46.708
- Here, I, uh, brought you a present.
- Really?

06:46.878 --> 06:49.745
Yeah, it's one of those Cuban fellas
you like puffing on.

06:50.549 --> 06:53.746
- That's very sweet, thank you.
- You're very welcome.

06:56.922 --> 06:59.390
Did you do something different
with your hair? Looks nice.

06:59.558 --> 07:01.048
Don't get me started.

07:04.162 --> 07:06.756
So when did you find out
about your dad?

07:06.932 --> 07:08.832
- Find out what?
- That he's gay.

07:09.000 --> 07:10.160
My dad's not gay.

07:10.335 --> 07:11.825
You sure? My dad is.

07:12.537 --> 07:15.097
- No kidding?
- Yep.

07:16.041 --> 07:17.599
You smell like strawberries.

07:18.276 --> 07:19.436
It's my lip gloss.

07:19.811 --> 07:21.438
Cool. Does it taste like it smells?

07:21.947 --> 07:23.676
- You wanna find out?
- Sure.

07:29.187 --> 07:30.654
Mm.

07:37.329 --> 07:39.854
Can we watch a soccer game
instead of basketball?

07:40.398 --> 07:42.332
What are you, nuts?

07:42.801 --> 07:45.269
Sophie says soccer's
the most popular sport in the world.

07:45.437 --> 07:48.235
Well, then they don't need us
to watch it.

07:52.143 --> 07:54.043
You know what would be a good idea?

07:54.212 --> 07:57.272
Maple-syrup lip gloss.

08:01.253 --> 08:02.777
Your mom will be here any minute.

08:02.954 --> 08:04.717
- I told you to get ready.
- I'm ready.

08:04.890 --> 08:06.221
- Did you do your homework?
- No.

08:07.592 --> 08:09.651
Jake, I promised your mother
you'd have it done.

08:09.828 --> 08:12.626
Well, next time you'll know better.

08:22.040 --> 08:25.305
I think Jake has a thing
for your boyfriend's daughter.

08:27.612 --> 08:29.512
He's not my boyfriend. We're friends.

08:29.681 --> 08:31.410
Friends, huh?

08:31.583 --> 08:34.780
Alan, when an intelligent, successful,
attractive man...

08:34.953 --> 08:36.944
...wants to be friends with you...

08:37.489 --> 08:39.684
...something is amiss.

08:40.258 --> 08:44.058
Excuse me, but if Greg were to be
interested in anybody around here...

08:44.229 --> 08:45.287
...it would be you.

08:45.931 --> 08:48.195
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

08:49.768 --> 08:51.633
- What are you talking about?
- Heh.

08:51.803 --> 08:55.830
Come on, Charlie, you got to admit
you put out a special kind of vibe.

08:58.043 --> 08:59.510
You don't mean special,
you mean:

08:59.678 --> 09:01.270
Special.

09:03.415 --> 09:04.780
And I don't.

09:05.584 --> 09:08.417
You're 40 years old,
you've never been married...

09:08.587 --> 09:11.522
...you play the piano, you're meticulous
about your appearance...

09:11.690 --> 09:16.787
Hey, hey, hey, I've got a riding crop in
my bathroom that never touched a horse.

09:17.762 --> 09:20.356
Your bathroom also has two kinds
of skin moisturizer...

09:20.532 --> 09:24.491
...various hair gels, colognes,
powders and emollients.

09:24.669 --> 09:26.296
I only have one moisturizer.

09:26.471 --> 09:29.304
The other one is a sun block
with moisturizer.

09:29.507 --> 09:31.998
Ah, right, you need that sun block...

09:32.177 --> 09:34.577
...for when you lean out the front door
to get the paper.

09:35.947 --> 09:38.108
There's no shade out there in the morning,
Alan.

09:38.283 --> 09:39.511
Uh-huh.

09:39.684 --> 09:43.211
Excuse me for not wanting to spend
my 50s looking like a catcher's mitt.

09:43.822 --> 09:48.259
All right, all right, let's, uh, scoot away
from the Clinique counter for a minute...

09:51.796 --> 09:54.822
...and, uh, discuss some of the people
you've attracted.

09:55.000 --> 09:57.696
Okay. You're thinking about that time
at the House of Blues...

09:57.869 --> 10:00.531
...and there's no way I could've known
that was a guy.

10:01.406 --> 10:03.897
He was 6'2"
and could palm a medicine ball.

10:06.378 --> 10:10.280
I was drunk, he was tucked, taped
and gorgeous.

10:11.916 --> 10:15.408
Charlie, you brought home a dude
in a dress.

10:16.287 --> 10:18.847
A dude who wanted to be a woman...

10:19.024 --> 10:22.187
...which means he was looking
for a straight man, which is me.

10:23.061 --> 10:29.057
Rationalize it any way you want, but he still
sends you flowers on valentine's Day.

10:31.002 --> 10:33.527
Only because I was a gentleman.

10:35.440 --> 10:38.068
- So how was your weekend?
- It was okay.

10:38.243 --> 10:40.768
- We went sailing.
- Oh, how nice.

10:40.945 --> 10:43.675
- What else?
- Nothing.

10:48.620 --> 10:51.282
Oh, yeah, I think Dad's gay now.

10:52.257 --> 10:54.817
That was a red light, Mom.

10:58.096 --> 11:00.326
So, Charlie, I haven't seen you
in a while.

11:00.498 --> 11:02.090
What's up?

11:02.267 --> 11:05.668
Why does something have to be up?
Can't I just drop by and say hello?

11:06.004 --> 11:09.167
For $350 an hour,
you can say anything you want.

11:10.108 --> 11:13.669
Okay, well, there is something
that's been kind of gnawing at me.

11:13.845 --> 11:15.005
Mm-hm.

11:15.180 --> 11:17.341
Well, this friend of mine...

11:17.515 --> 11:18.743
Your friend?

11:21.186 --> 11:22.653
Yeah, a friend.

11:23.321 --> 11:24.982
It's your money, Charlie.

11:25.390 --> 11:27.790
Okay. Okay.

11:28.493 --> 11:32.520
Is it possible that I could be gay
without knowing it?

11:34.632 --> 11:35.929
Why do you ask?

11:36.101 --> 11:38.592
Well, my brother's got this friend...

11:38.770 --> 11:41.830
We're talking $ 7 a minute.

11:42.006 --> 11:44.668
No, no, no, this friend's real.

11:44.843 --> 11:48.904
He's gay, and apparently
I triggered his gaydar.

11:49.881 --> 11:52.509
- Well, I can understand that.
- You can?

11:53.284 --> 11:55.047
You can?

11:56.421 --> 12:00.050
Let me ask you something, Charlie.
Have you ever had sex with a man?

12:00.225 --> 12:02.887
No. No. Absolutely not.

12:09.501 --> 12:12.732
All right, I copped a feel once,
but I was drunk and he had breasts.

12:20.645 --> 12:24.240
- Hey, is Jake ready?
- Jake, your father's here.

12:25.183 --> 12:27.708
- He'll be right out.
- Good.

12:29.954 --> 12:31.285
So, uh, how've you been?

12:31.689 --> 12:33.919
- Good. And you?
- Good.

12:37.128 --> 12:39.221
Oh, come here. I am so proud of you.

12:40.298 --> 12:41.959
Thanks. What did I do?

12:42.467 --> 12:44.264
Alan, you don't have to hide anymore.

12:44.435 --> 12:48.235
Jake told me all about you and Greg. I want
you to know I completely support you.

12:49.073 --> 12:52.270
- Oh, gee, Judith, um...
- Is that him in the car? Gee, he's cute.

12:52.710 --> 12:57.147
Hello. That must be his daughter.
I can see why Jake has a crush on her.

12:57.315 --> 13:00.113
- Yeah, we're taking them to the movies...
- This makes so much sense.

13:00.285 --> 13:02.810
I can't believe I didn't see this
when we were married.

13:02.987 --> 13:04.648
- See what?
- Oh, come on, Alan.

13:04.823 --> 13:09.783
You picking out my clothes,
your neat fetish, the show tunes, the sex.

13:10.728 --> 13:12.958
- There was no sex.
- Exactly.

13:13.131 --> 13:16.794
All those years you were so miserable,
and look at you now. You're glowing.

13:16.968 --> 13:21.064
No, wait. Hang on a second.
The reason that there was no...

13:22.073 --> 13:23.973
- Really, I'm glowing?
- Well, yeah.

13:24.142 --> 13:27.942
To think, all this time I've been blaming
myself because the marriage didn't work.

13:28.112 --> 13:30.478
No, I'm pretty sure
you've been blaming me.

13:30.648 --> 13:35.312
It was nobody's fault, Alan. I'm just so glad
you've finally accepted who you really are.

13:35.920 --> 13:37.820
Hey, Dad.
- Hey, buddy.

13:37.989 --> 13:39.513
Hey, Sophie.

13:39.691 --> 13:41.716
You boys are so cute
with your double dates.

13:42.460 --> 13:44.121
- Listen, Judith...
- I almost forgot.

13:44.295 --> 13:47.958
Your mother told me to tell you
that she's behind you a hundred percent.

13:48.132 --> 13:52.296
- When did you talk to my mother?
- Well, after Jake told me, I called her.

13:52.871 --> 13:55.203
- Why?
- We had a little bet. It's not important.

13:56.674 --> 13:58.107
Bye-bye.

14:01.212 --> 14:04.113
I mean, okay, I do care
about my appearance.

14:04.282 --> 14:07.649
Plus I've got mother issues
and a bit of a flair for interior design.

14:09.220 --> 14:11.415
You know, sconces, throw pillows,
bric-a-brac.

14:11.589 --> 14:12.954
Mm.

14:13.391 --> 14:16.155
But when it comes to penises,
I am pretty clear...

14:16.327 --> 14:19.421
...that the only one I want winking at me
is my own.

14:21.532 --> 14:24.330
Who are you trying to convince here,
Charlie? Me or you?

14:24.502 --> 14:26.993
You, and then I want you
to convince me.

14:28.339 --> 14:29.601
Why do you need convincing?

14:30.942 --> 14:33.240
- Wow, good question.
- Thanks.

14:33.411 --> 14:36.437
Once in a while I get a little wood
on the ball.

14:37.315 --> 14:40.182
I mean, it has been suggested to me
that all of my womanizing...

14:40.351 --> 14:42.911
...is just my way of overcompensating.

14:43.087 --> 14:44.384
Who suggested that?

14:45.590 --> 14:49.048
Uh, mostly the women
I was overcompensating on top of.

14:50.328 --> 14:55.732
Well, this is a very interesting area,
but I'm afraid we're out of time.

14:56.534 --> 14:58.900
What? No, no, we can't stop here.

14:59.070 --> 15:03.063
- I have a patient waiting, Charlie.
- Right. Hold on a sec.

15:06.144 --> 15:09.602
Here, go get yourself something to eat.
Come back in an hour.

15:13.584 --> 15:15.814
Okay, new clock.

15:17.822 --> 15:21.815
My mom took my temperature the baby way
till I was 8 years old.

15:48.886 --> 15:49.910
Hey, Dad.

15:50.088 --> 15:53.080
- Yeah?
- It's okay if I'm not gay, right?

16:00.932 --> 16:04.561
Jake, listen, you and I
need to clear the air about something.

16:04.736 --> 16:06.897
- After I call Sophie.
- You just saw her.

16:07.071 --> 16:11.201
- What do you need to talk about?
- Boy-girl stuff. You wouldn't understand.

16:14.545 --> 16:16.513
Hey, Alan. Your mom called.

16:16.714 --> 16:19.615
- She gave me the news.
- Oh, God.

16:20.184 --> 16:22.084
Come here.

16:22.854 --> 16:24.287
I'm proud of you, Zippy.

16:25.857 --> 16:28.291
The world is a happier place
once you figure out...

16:28.459 --> 16:30.359
...whether you're the pin or the cushion.

16:33.164 --> 16:34.791
Good night.

16:41.606 --> 16:42.732
Charlie?

16:43.574 --> 16:47.066
- Yeah?
- I think I might be gay.

16:48.613 --> 16:50.638
What did you do, Alan?

16:51.416 --> 16:55.318
Nothing, but I'm starting
to put the pieces together.

16:55.787 --> 16:58.654
Which piece did you put where, Alan?

17:00.425 --> 17:01.449
I'm just thinking that...

17:02.827 --> 17:04.886
...I've failed at every
female relationship I've had.

17:05.063 --> 17:07.827
Oh, come on, that makes every man
in the world gay.

17:10.368 --> 17:12.233
Let me finish.

17:12.403 --> 17:15.566
I've been unappy for most of my life.

17:15.740 --> 17:19.107
I've never really fit in anywhere...

17:19.277 --> 17:23.213
...and now, suddenly, I'm happy.

17:23.381 --> 17:27.181
Some might even say I'm glowing.

17:27.785 --> 17:32.313
There is a big leap
between glowing and flaming.

17:34.659 --> 17:38.026
I'm just saying that this friendship
with Greg has been so easy...

17:38.196 --> 17:44.692
...and fun, and everybody else
just seems happier thinking I'm gay.

17:45.036 --> 17:46.230
Maybe that's the answer.

17:46.771 --> 17:48.136
What was the question?

17:49.407 --> 17:51.398
Who is Alan Harper?

17:51.709 --> 17:53.074
That's easy.

17:53.244 --> 17:54.871
Alan Harper is an idiot.

17:56.547 --> 17:59.311
Why is my sexuality
so threatening to you?

18:01.252 --> 18:03.550
It's not threatening. I am not threatened.

18:03.721 --> 18:05.655
- Is that so?
- Okay.

18:05.823 --> 18:07.017
- Okay.
- Hmm?

18:07.191 --> 18:08.556
Now, you listen to me.

18:08.726 --> 18:11.820
You're not gay, I'm not gay,
nobody's gay.

18:11.996 --> 18:14.863
- Nobody's gay?
- Not in this house.

18:16.134 --> 18:17.761
Where are you going?

18:17.935 --> 18:19.800
I have to buy some new hair conditioner.

18:24.675 --> 18:27.303
- That was a good meeting tonight.
- Yeah, it was okay...

18:27.478 --> 18:29.969
...but some of those single moms
get real gossipy.

18:30.148 --> 18:32.048
Oh, oh, like, uh, Rebecca Milford:

18:32.216 --> 18:34.116
Yakety-yakety-yakety.

18:34.285 --> 18:36.150
And did you see what she had on?

18:36.320 --> 18:38.914
Who could miss it?
A woman that size should not wear paisley.

18:40.825 --> 18:43.794
- Okay, thanks for the ride.
- Oh, oh, no problem.

18:44.195 --> 18:46.288
We still taking the kids
to the mall Saturday?

18:46.464 --> 18:48.432
You kidding?
I'm taking Jake to the mall Friday...

18:48.599 --> 18:50.931
...so he can have cool clothes to wear
to the mall Saturday.

18:52.303 --> 18:56.535
So maybe I'll see you there Friday.
Okay, bye-bye.

18:58.576 --> 19:00.339
- Greg, wait.
- Yeah?

19:06.684 --> 19:08.811
- Alan?
- Yeah?

19:09.954 --> 19:11.478
What are you doing?

19:12.757 --> 19:16.158
Uh, I was just, you know...

19:16.427 --> 19:17.985
...checking.

19:18.162 --> 19:19.823
Checking what?

19:20.264 --> 19:21.561
Well, it's not important.

19:21.732 --> 19:25.498
I just thought, uh, that, you know,
possibly...

19:25.870 --> 19:27.997
...I might be...

19:28.906 --> 19:30.168
Never mind.

19:30.575 --> 19:31.974
Alan, you're not gay.

19:32.877 --> 19:34.538
Are you sure?

19:34.979 --> 19:36.913
Do you find me sexually attractive?

19:38.182 --> 19:40.844
- No.
- Do you find any man sexually attractive?

19:41.919 --> 19:45.013
No. Well, maybe George Clooney.

19:46.190 --> 19:47.418
Clooney doesn't count.

19:47.592 --> 19:50.823
Trust me, you're not gay.

19:52.897 --> 19:54.364
Okay.

19:55.066 --> 19:56.863
You seem disappointed.

19:58.669 --> 20:02.867
I just... I feel like
I'm letting a lot of people down.

20:04.008 --> 20:05.566
Alan...

20:06.477 --> 20:08.206
...it's okay to be straight.

20:09.247 --> 20:11.408
Yeah, I guess.

20:11.582 --> 20:15.541
So just to put all our cards on the table,
you're not at all attracted to me?

20:15.720 --> 20:18.951
No. You're not my type.
Now, Charlie on the other hand...

20:19.123 --> 20:23.116
- What about him?
- He's, uh, very pretty.

20:23.995 --> 20:25.223
Get out of my car.

20:25.630 --> 20:27.359
- What?
- You think Charlie's so pretty?

20:27.531 --> 20:30.762
- Go to the mall with Charlie.
- Oh, come on, Alan, we're friends.

20:30.935 --> 20:33.460
No, I'm always the friend.
Everybody wants Charlie.

20:33.638 --> 20:36.402
Alan, you're not gay.

20:36.574 --> 20:39.407
Yeah, well, there's
a principle involved. Good night.

20:43.614 --> 20:45.582
Suit yourself.

20:52.056 --> 20:53.455
Well...

20:54.325 --> 20:56.691
...at least I know who I am.

20:57.662 --> 21:00.688
A heterosexual nut job.

21:06.037 --> 21:08.096
I can't believe you broke up
with Sophie's dad.

21:09.573 --> 21:10.665
I didn't...

21:12.143 --> 21:13.542
I'm not...

21:15.346 --> 21:17.246
I'm sorry.

21:18.549 --> 21:20.346
You know what would help this room?

21:20.518 --> 21:23.180
Get rid of all these lamps
and put in some track lighting.

21:24.622 --> 21:26.317
Much more flattering.

21:29.560 --> 21:32.654
- What are you eating?
- Lip gloss.
